WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.345 --> 00:00:01.404
(mysterious music)

00:00:01.404 --> 00:00:03.583
- [Narrator] It starts
with a yes or question:

00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:05.061
Does she have a crush on me?

00:00:05.061 --> 00:00:06.934
Will I pass the test?

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:10.013
Will the Mets win the World Series?

00:00:10.013 --> 00:00:12.626
Well, they may not have
always predicted the truth.

00:00:12.626 --> 00:00:14.610
Magic Eight balls are actually inspired

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.860
by a real life clairvoyant.

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:21.225
- [Narrator] Do you want
to hear your fortune?

00:00:21.225 --> 00:00:22.205
(Greek inspired music)

00:00:22.205 --> 00:00:24.646
- [Narrator] In the 1940s, Mary
Carter was a popular medium

00:00:24.646 --> 00:00:27.517
best known for her mysterious
fortune-telling invention.

00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:29.384
It was called the Syco Slate.

00:00:29.384 --> 00:00:31.489
Essentially, a chalkboard with a cover.

00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:32.426
When the clients would visit,

00:00:32.426 --> 00:00:34.363
Mary would ask a question to the spirits.

00:00:34.363 --> 00:00:35.634
(scribbling)

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.762
The room would fill with
the sound of scribbling

00:00:37.762 --> 00:00:39.928
and then just like, poof, magic,

00:00:39.928 --> 00:00:41.777
Mary would reveal answers
from another world

00:00:41.777 --> 00:00:44.330
mysteriously written on the chalkboard.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.920
Mary's son, Albert, was
inspired by his mother

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.476
and created his own truth seeking device.

00:00:49.476 --> 00:00:51.234
But this time you didn't need a psychic

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:52.573
to tell you your fortune.

00:00:52.573 --> 00:00:53.858
(big band music)

00:00:53.858 --> 00:00:55.361
He put a pair of worded dice

00:00:55.361 --> 00:00:57.005
inside a tube filled with molasses.

00:00:57.005 --> 00:00:59.329
Each end was clear so you
could read the answers.

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:00.582
Sound familiar?

00:01:00.582 --> 00:01:01.470
(ding)

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.854
Albert hit the streets.

00:01:02.854 --> 00:01:04.011
He partnered with a
couple local businessmen

00:01:04.011 --> 00:01:05.389
and opened a novelty company

00:01:05.389 --> 00:01:08.225
where they specialized in the
Miracle Home Fortune-Teller.

00:01:08.225 --> 00:01:09.127
After he died,

00:01:09.127 --> 00:01:10.374
Albert's partners took over

00:01:10.374 --> 00:01:12.069
and redesigned the project
(scribbling)

00:01:12.069 --> 00:01:13.130
numerous times.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.404
They ended up with crystal ball-like shape

00:01:15.404 --> 00:01:16.667
with a die in the middle.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.558
And a billiards company took note.

00:01:18.558 --> 00:01:19.862
They needed a promotional item

00:01:19.862 --> 00:01:21.274
so they replaced the crystal ball

00:01:21.274 --> 00:01:24.001
with the iconic black eight ball.

00:01:24.001 --> 00:01:27.382
The promotion was so
successful that they rebranded

00:01:27.382 --> 00:01:28.751
the magic eight ball.

00:01:28.751 --> 00:01:31.447
This time marketing it
as a fortune-telling toy.

00:01:31.447 --> 00:01:32.434
(cash register dings)

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:35.106
Today, kids are still
using magic eight balls

00:01:35.106 --> 00:01:37.058
to ask for their fortunes.

00:01:37.058 --> 00:01:38.065
And for that,

00:01:38.065 --> 00:01:40.092
you can thank Mary the clairvoyant.

00:01:40.092 --> 00:01:41.592
- [Woman] Ah, yes.

